  "content": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Plain summary"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The work is a strong candidate package, not a finished printer conversion. It is built to make the next session safer and more reproducible. It does not imply that the printer has already been changed."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Current Orca and print state"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This laptop's OrcaSlicer 2.4.2 user configuration now has eight reviewed T300 presets installed. New projects default to the audited zero-hop runtime machine. A separate 0.4 mm collision-clearance machine variant is available but is not the default."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Four editable review projects are in Downloads/T300-Orca-Review-20260805. They are not final print files. The first-layer project waits for machine commissioning, the bracket waits for orange PLA calibration, and both Frieren projects wait for the chosen filament calibration plus a successful bracket validation print."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Current physical state"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The printer remains on Comgrow/Sovol firmware 1.5.2 and patched Klipper 0.12.0."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The backed-up printer USB has been repurposed as a verified Armbian recovery USB with the T300 recovery overlay installed."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "No mainline files have been written to eMMC."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "No MCU has been flashed."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "No new movement, homing, probing, or heating was triggered during this documentation and commit pass."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The purchased GerGo macro remains private and is not included in the public repository."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Current repository state"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The printer repo contains the public mainline candidate, policy code, test harnesses, staging tools, recovery tools, runtime configs, docs, lockfiles, and portable Orca machine, filament, and process profiles."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "GitHub origin/main includes the original mainline candidate at commit 0590c50. The pressure-advance, extrusion-accounting, status, and Orca refinement described in this Dossier is the current local release candidate until its final commit is published."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Ignored local caches still contain backups, camera recordings, generated files, and private material. They are intentionally outside the commit."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The Dossier project lives in dossier/ as data-only project content. It contains no Dossier Engine runtime source."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What approval should mean"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Approval should mean: the documented design is coherent enough to proceed to recovery preparation and attended commissioning. It should not mean: skip backup, skip screen identity proof, skip physical inspection, or let automation command the printer without you."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Main open risks"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The T300 stock bed may still have physical unevenness. Software can compensate only so far."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The removable steel sheet still has no real presence sensor. The checkmark workflow reduces user error but cannot detect a sheet removed after confirmation."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Frieren stringing is mainly filament and slicer tuning work, not a firmware migration problem by itself."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Powerline network stability during long prints remains a home electrical/network issue, so camera/timelapse failures must not affect print motion or safety."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mainline migration still needs hardware commissioning evidence on the actual printer."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
